# Video. Vercel hosts none of it -- the deployment is a rewrite rule and
# nothing else. The bytes come from the Supabase bucket.
clips/
out/
agents/
prospects/
needs_attention/
*.mp4

# Secrets and leads. A .vercelignore takes precedence over .gitignore, so
# these are NOT covered by the gitignore rules that cover them for git --
# and check_pii.py only sees what git would publish, never what the Vercel
# CLI would upload. Deploying is a second publishing boundary with its own
# ignore file, and it has to be spelled out here or it is not enforced.
.env
.env.*
scraper/
outreach/
agents.txt
property_email.txt

# Noise.
__pycache__/
tests/
# dashboard.py holds no PII -- it renders it, never stores it -- so git
# keeps it and check_pii.py scans it. It has no role in a deployment that
# is a rewrite rule and nothing else, and its whole purpose is to serve
# agent names, phones and emails over a socket. The one host in this
# project where those two facts could meet does not get the file.
dashboard.py

# Syncthing. .stfolder is its per-folder marker and .stversions its trash;
# neither belongs in the repo, and a *.sync-conflict-* copy is a stale duplicate
# of a file that is already committed -- see PROGRESS.md on the 2026-09-02 pass.
.stfolder/
.stversions/
*.sync-conflict-*
